<title>UK: Nobo says may sell co, warns on profits.</title>
<headline>Nobo says may sell co, warns on profits.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>British office products company Nobo Group Plc said on Friday it was in talks that could lead to an offer being made for the firm at a level of about 138.5p per share.</p>
<p>Nobo also warned that its pre-tax profits excluding exceptional costs for the year to May 2 would be about two-thirds of last year's 2.93 million stg.  </p>
<p>The company cited weaker-than-expected demand across the UK office products sector.</p>
<p>Nobo did not give further details of its talks.</p>
<p>The company's shares sank 14.5p to 124 by 0850 GMT.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
